  "script": "A guy came into my store returning a five-hundred-dollar espresso machine, insisting it 'just stopped working' after three weeks, demanding a brand new replacement instead of the free repair our policy actually offers. I processed it because that's the job, but our warranty system logs a serial number on every claim, and something about his story felt rehearsed. I searched it. It was the same serial number, four returns, four different store locations, four different months, always the same claim, always a brand new box walking back out the door with him. He wasn't buying new machines and returning broken ones \u2014 he'd found one machine that never left his house, and just kept 'returning' it for a fresh one every time the warranty reset. I flagged the account company-wide with the pattern attached. He came back a fifth time, receipt in hand, and the register simply refused the return \u2014 right in front of the whole line, with his own serial number printed on the screen.",
